eval.summary:
T1-go-opus1 passes every check. Hidden T1 is 14/14 on darwin and 14/14 on linux on the first run, so there was nothing to rerun and no flakiness was observed. score.py gives all_pass true on both platforms with regressed 0. Fixed is 8/8 on darwin (6/6 excluding the unproven darwin nested_shell checks) and 6/6 on linux. The full 2.4.2 harness is 139/139 on both platforms and `go test ./...` exits 0. The frozen copy rebuilt from source with all four targets, including windows-x64. Its darwin sha256 (457ce20f...) and linux-arm64 sha256 (4ae668ad...) equal the implementer's, and the frozen and workspace dist trees are byte-identical. The base tree digest equals BASE.json. The pin check matched BASE.json (T4 seeded-* exit 1, base-* exit 0, digests equal). One caveat is that the transcript audit returned VERDICT SUSPECT, with 24 of 78 calls flagged. I inspected those calls by hand and judged the cell not contaminated. The flagged calls were:
- the first `cd` into the workspace, made from the repository-root cwd;
- Go module cache, own scratch, docker and ps commands run at the repository-root cwd;
- references to the workspace's parent directory;
- a read of the implementer's own persisted tool output;
- one `ps` listing that printed executable names of other cells' processes. It showed no file content.
No call read the repository prototypes, hidden material, seeded or base trees, or another workspace's files. The workspace was fresh (manifest created 2026-10-09T05:01:14Z, and the implementer ran `git init` itself). My check looked only at tool inputs and the flagged outputs. The audit used the implementer's agent transcript from the orchestrator's workflow session directory, matched by its meta description impl-T1-go-opus1. The diff against base 84c7665 touches 9 files in prototypes/go: internal/run/run_unix.go and the group_{linux,darwin,other}.go files, new tests, and REPORT.md. Evidence is in <home>/GitRepos/heimdall/tests/evidence/artifacts/g02-r4/x2/runs/T1-go-opus1/ (out/ from the implementer, results/ from me). I scrubbed it (home path to <home>, repo to <repo>, hidden dir to <hidden>) and scan-home.py exits 0 on it. Cleanup ran for real, and the builds are kept in /tmp/x2ws-4c8e064b/eval/out/ with SHA256SUMS.
